What?!

265
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:26,645
We're going to be roomies!

266
00:11:26,685 --> 00:11:27,895
Come on.

267
00:11:37,113 --> 00:11:38,448
You slept out here?

268
00:11:38,490 --> 00:11:40,741
Well, Amy kept kicking
me in her sleep,

269
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:43,911
yelling, "Myron, get off."

270
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:45,872
But, uh, we're getting rid
of her, right?

271
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:48,082
Rach, please tell me
we're getting rid of her.

272
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:49,668
Joey, I can't do that.

273
00:11:49,708 --> 00:11:51,211
Oh, come on!

274
00:11:51,252 --> 00:11:53,004
Last night I was
finishing off a pizza,

275
00:11:53,046 --> 00:11:54,673
and she said,
"A moment on the lips,

276
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:56,049
forever on the hips."

277
00:11:57,509 --> 00:11:59,678
I don't need that kind
of talk in my house!

278
00:11:59,718 --> 00:12:01,221
Well, Joey,

279
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:02,972
look, I know
that she's difficult,

280
00:12:03,014 --> 00:12:05,433
but I think it's really good
that she's here.

281
00:12:06,476 --> 00:12:08,687
'Cause we'll appreciate
it more when she's gone?

282
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:09,937
I, wh...?

283
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,566
No, it's just,
look, you know,

284
00:12:12,607 --> 00:12:15,610
when I first moved to this city,
I was a lot like her.

285
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:17,654
I was spoiled, self-centered,

286
00:12:17,696 --> 00:12:20,198
and you guys
really took care of me.

287
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:22,283
Yeah, Monica made us.

288
00:12:23,368 --> 00:12:25,579
Well, whatever,
I really appreciate it,

289
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:28,956
'cause I don't think I would be
the person that I am today

290
00:12:28,998 --> 00:12:30,458
if it wasn't for you guys.

291
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:33,044
See, I want to help Amy

292
00:12:33,086 --> 00:12:34,795
the way you guys helped me,

293
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:37,090
and I know it's going to take
patience, but that's okay.

294
00:12:38,091 --> 00:12:39,175
Good morning.

295
00:12:39,217 --> 00:12:40,968
( groans )

296
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:42,637
RACHEL:
Amy,

297
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:44,264
that what I was supposed
to wear today.

298
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:45,640
That's why I hung it
on the door.

299
00:12:45,682 --> 00:12:48,393
Oh, sweetie,
you can't pull this off.

300
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:55,275
Amy, you know what,
I was thinking that, um,

301
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:57,652
maybe now would be
a good time for us
to sit down

302
00:12:57,694 --> 00:12:59,654
and, uh, you know,
talk about your future.

303
00:12:59,696 --> 00:13:01,239
Oh, I can't, honey.

304
00:13:01,281 --> 00:13:02,823
I'm going to go
get my eyebrows shaped.

305
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:05,368
I am not happy.

306
00:13:06,369 --> 00:13:07,995
Uh.

307
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:09,623
Sure you want
to eat that?

308
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:14,669
I'm curvy and I like it!

309
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:20,174
Hi.

310
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:21,426
Hi.
Hey.

311
00:13:21,468 --> 00:13:23,470
I just I had
the worst anniversary ever.

312
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:24,763
CHANDLER:
I doubt that.

313
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:26,640
Tell her about us last year.

314
00:13:26,681 --> 00:13:29,850
Oh, well, I bought Chandler
a $500 watch,

315
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:32,145
and he wrote me a rap song.

316
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:35,189
Seriously?

317
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:36,899
Word.

318
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:40,445
Well, mine was worse than that.

319
00:13:40,487 --> 00:13:42,196
Well, what happened?

320
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:44,699
We were at the game, and this
guy proposed to his girlfriend

321
00:13:44,741 --> 00:13:45,742
on the big screen thing.

322
00:13:45,784 --> 00:13:47,452
Oh, that is so tacky.

323
00:13:47,494 --> 00:13:49,078
Well, that's what I said.

324
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:51,998
But it turns out Mike
was planning on proposing to me

325
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:53,500
that same way last night.

326
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:54,501
Oh, my God.

327
00:13:54,542 --> 00:13:55,669
Mike was going to propose?

328
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:56,919
Phoebe, that's huge.

329
00:13:56,961 --> 00:13:58,004
Well, do you want
to marry him?

330
00:13:58,045 --> 00:13:59,756
Yeah, I really do, yes.

331
00:13:59,798 --> 00:14:02,676
But after I dumped on the way
he was going to propose to me,

332
00:14:02,717 --> 00:14:05,052
I don't think he's ever going
to ask again.

333
00:14:05,094 --> 00:14:07,555
I mean, I said no in Barbados,
and now this.

334
00:14:07,597 --> 00:14:09,349
She's right.
If I were a guy and...

335
00:14:14,729 --> 00:14:18,399
Did I just say,
"If I were a guy"?

336
00:14:18,441 --> 00:14:20,735
Maybe you don't need him
to propose to you.

337
00:14:20,777 --> 00:14:22,570
Maybe you could propose to him.

338
00:14:22,612 --> 00:14:24,489
Oh, I don't know.
I don't know.

339
00:14:24,531 --> 00:14:26,449
Isn't that a little desperate?

340
00:14:26,491 --> 00:14:27,826
I proposed to Chandler.

341
00:14:31,705 --> 00:14:34,541
All right, moving on.

342
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:36,209
Well, I don't think
it was desperate.

343
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:37,377
I think it was amazing.

344
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:38,545
Thank you.

345
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,463
Well, do you think
I should propose?

346
00:14:40,505 --> 00:14:42,632
I think it could
be kind of great.

347
00:14:42,674 --> 00:14:43,633
Absolutely.

348
00:14:43,675 --> 00:14:45,134
You'll love the feeling.

349
00:14:45,176 --> 00:14:47,178
There's nothing like it.

350
00:14:49,222 --> 00:14:50,640
Okay. Okay.

351
00:14:50,682 --> 00:14:52,266
So, how should I do it?

352
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:54,728
How about at a game
on the big screen?

353
00:14:54,769 --> 00:14:57,814
( gasps ):
How about at
a Foot Locker?

354
00:14:58,815 --> 00:15:00,775
What? What,
he obviously thinks

355
00:15:00,817 --> 00:15:03,152
that's a nice way
to be proposed to.

356
00:15:03,194 --> 00:15:05,154
Plus, he'd never suspect it.

357
00:15:05,196 --> 00:15:07,448
Yeah, that does
make sense. Okay.

358
00:15:07,490 --> 00:15:09,868
Now, would-would you two
like that?

359
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:11,327
Sounds good to me.

360
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:13,621
But what would a guy think?

361
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:18,626
Uh, Nana's on the phone.

362
00:15:18,668 --> 00:15:22,463
Oh, that's interesting,
since she died seven years ago.

363
00:15:22,505 --> 00:15:24,340
She did?

364
00:15:24,382 --> 00:15:27,134
Who got her condo in Boca?

365
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:29,721
Hello.

366
00:15:29,763 --> 00:15:30,722
Oh.

367
00:15:30,764 --> 00:15:31,765
It's our nanny.

368
00:15:31,806 --> 00:15:33,474
Hi.

369
00:15:33,516 --> 00:15:36,853
Oh, God, I hope
you feel better.

370
00:15:36,895 --> 00:15:38,688
Okay, bye.

371
00:15:38,730 --> 00:15:40,857
That's Molly, she's sick.

372
00:15:40,899 --> 00:15:42,316
Can you watch Emma today?

373
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:44,277
I can't. I have
back-to-back classes.

374
00:15:44,318 --> 00:15:45,695
Did Molly say what she had

375
00:15:45,737 --> 00:15:47,488
because my throat's
been hurting.

376
00:15:47,530 --> 00:15:49,490
Menstrual cramps.

377
00:15:50,533 --> 00:15:53,787
I don't think
that's what this is.

378
00:15:53,828 --> 00:15:56,539
Can any of you watch Emma?

379
00:15:56,581 --> 00:15:58,124
No, sorry.
No, sorry, sweetie.

380
00:15:58,165 --> 00:16:00,835
No, I've got work,
and then I'm proposing and...

381
00:16:00,877 --> 00:16:01,836
Oh, great.

382
00:16:01,878 --> 00:16:03,504
Shoot! What are we going to do?

383
00:16:03,546 --> 00:16:04,798
Well, I could do it.

384
00:16:04,839 --> 00:16:06,716
Well, actually...

385
00:16:06,758 --> 00:16:09,009
Uh, can I talk to you
for a sec?

386
00:16:09,051 --> 00:16:10,386
Yeah.

387
00:16:10,428 --> 00:16:13,807
Um, I do not want her
baby-sitting our child.

388
00:16:13,848 --> 00:16:15,266
Why not?

389
00:16:15,308 --> 00:16:17,560
Well, for one thing,
she keeps calling her "Ella."

390
00:16:17,602 --> 00:16:19,646
Ella's a nice name.

391
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:21,063
Fine, we'll call
the next one Ella!

392
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:22,356
Next, the next one?

393
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:23,691
Okay, uh...

394
00:16:23,733 --> 00:16:28,028
Um, I don't want her
watching our baby.

395
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:31,031
Ross, I am trying to help
her become a better person.

396
00:16:31,073 --> 00:16:33,033
This is a huge
breakthrough for her.

397
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:35,369
She just offered
to do something

398
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:37,204
for another human being.

399
00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:38,372
Look, look,
I-I don't know...

400
00:16:38,414 --> 00:16:39,958
Ross, I'm telling you,

401
00:16:39,998 --> 00:16:42,710
she's giving up getting
her eyebrows shaped

402
00:16:42,752 --> 00:16:44,128
to do this, all right?

403
00:16:44,170 --> 00:16:46,631
Do you understand
how important that is

404
00:16:46,673 --> 00:16:47,966
in our world?

405
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:52,303
Um, listen, I...
I couldn't help but overhear

406
00:16:52,345 --> 00:16:54,180
'cause I was trying to.

407
00:16:55,222 --> 00:16:56,766
Listen,
let me do this.

408
00:16:56,808 --> 00:16:59,185
I-I really want
to help you guys out,

409
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:02,104
and plus, Rachel's been
so wonderful to me.

410
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:06,066
Absolutely.

411
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:07,318
Oh, great.

412
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:08,820
So, how much does it pay?

413
00:17:15,618 --> 00:17:17,077
Hey, Joe.

414
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:18,788
How's the second draft
of the letter coming?

415
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:19,831
Great. I'm finished.

416
00:17:19,873 --> 00:17:20,915
In fact,
I just dropped it off

417
00:17:20,957 --> 00:17:23,334
at the agency.

418
00:17:23,376 --> 00:17:24,961
You dropped it off?

419
00:17:25,003 --> 00:17:25,920
Yeah.

420
00:17:25,962 --> 00:17:27,005
Can we read it?

421
00:17:27,046 --> 00:17:28,088
Can you print out
another copy?

422
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:30,049
No can do, amigo.

423
00:17:31,592 --> 00:17:32,927
No, I didn't use a computer.

424
00:17:32,969 --> 00:17:34,762
It felt more personal
to handwrite it.

425
00:17:34,804 --> 00:17:35,847
( groans )

426
00:17:35,889 --> 00:17:37,598
You handwrote it?

427
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:38,933
Yeah, and don't worry.

428
00:17:38,975 --> 00:17:41,101
I didn't try to sound smart
at all.

429
00:17:42,144 --> 00:17:43,437
See you later.

430
00:17:43,479 --> 00:17:44,772
Oh, my God.
Oh, my God.

431
00:17:44,814 --> 00:17:46,941
That letter is going
to go in our file.

432
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:49,443
We're never going
to get a kid.

433
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:51,696
No, we're gonna...
we're gonna be

434
00:17:51,738 --> 00:17:55,324
one of those old couples
that collects orchids
or-or has a lot of birds.

435
00:17:55,366 --> 00:17:56,826
It's okay. It's okay.

436
00:17:56,868 --> 00:17:58,953
You know what,
I will just call the agency

437
00:17:58,995 --> 00:18:00,830
and tell them
to throw out the letter.

438
00:18:00,872 --> 00:18:02,540
Okay, good.

439
00:18:02,582 --> 00:18:05,668
Hello.
This is Chandler Bing.

440
00:18:05,710 --> 00:18:07,003
Somebody just dropped off

441
00:18:07,045 --> 00:18:09,171
a handwritten
recommendation letter and...

442
00:18:09,213 --> 00:18:14,010
Uh-huh.
Uh-huh.

443
00:18:14,052 --> 00:18:15,636
Okay.

444
00:18:16,721 --> 00:18:19,557
Thank you.
Good-bye.

445
00:18:19,599 --> 00:18:21,350
Oh, we're screwed, aren't we?

446
00:18:21,392 --> 00:18:24,478
You know what, just tell me
on the way to the bird store.

447
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:26,981
They loved it.

448
00:18:27,023 --> 00:18:28,148
What?

449
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:29,692
They thought
it was very smart of us

450
00:18:29,734 --> 00:18:31,736
to have a child write
the recommendation letter.

451
00:18:31,778 --> 00:18:34,864
They thought
Joey was a child?

452
00:18:34,906 --> 00:18:38,076
She guessed eight, nine,
based on his drawings.

453
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:42,413
AMY:
Hi.

454
00:18:42,455 --> 00:18:44,164
MONICA:
Hey, what did you guys do today?

455
00:18:44,206 --> 00:18:46,208
Ella wanted to go out,

456
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:49,045
so we went shopping
and got some sushi.

457
00:18:49,087 --> 00:18:50,922
That sounds like fun.

458
00:18:50,964 --> 00:18:52,673
Yeah, not really.

459
00:18:52,715 --> 00:18:54,341
Babies are dull.

460
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:56,844
Hey.

461
00:18:56,886 --> 00:18:58,679
Hi. How's my girl?

462
00:18:58,721 --> 00:18:59,973
I'm fine.

463
00:19:00,014 --> 00:19:02,058
And...

464
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:04,644
I got you a present for
letting me stay with you.

465
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:06,687
Ready?

466
00:19:06,729 --> 00:19:07,897
Yes.

467
00:19:07,939 --> 00:19:09,983
Ta-da!

468
00:19:11,025 --> 00:19:13,861
You pierced her ears?

469
00:19:13,903 --> 00:19:15,321
Doesn't it make her
nose look smaller?

470
00:19:15,362 --> 00:19:17,115
( shrieks )

471
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:25,873
How could you do this
without telling me?

472
00:19:25,915 --> 00:19:27,541
Well, if I had told you,
then it wouldn't have been

473
00:19:27,583 --> 00:19:29,376
a surprise, now, would it?

474
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:30,753
( moans )

475
00:19:30,795 --> 00:19:32,505
I think she looks cute.

476
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:35,716
But I am wrong.

477
00:19:35,758 --> 00:19:36,884
Oh, my God.

478
00:19:36,926 --> 00:19:38,886
Oh, my God,
here comes Ross.

479
00:19:38,928 --> 00:19:40,680
He is going to flip out.

480
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:43,432
Why, did something happen
to his falafel cart?

481
00:19:43,474 --> 00:19:45,810
Hey, guys.
Hi, Ross.

482
00:19:45,852 --> 00:19:47,603
Ross.
Hi, Emma.

483
00:19:48,646 --> 00:19:50,606
Oh, why is she wearing her hat
so low?

484
00:19:50,648 --> 00:19:51,774
She can barely see.

485
00:19:51,816 --> 00:19:53,734
I don't really
want her to see.

486
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:56,863
Why not?

487
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:58,238
MONICA:
Well, because

488
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:00,074
there's so many terrible sights
in this world.

489
00:20:00,116 --> 00:20:01,492
Like war.

490
00:20:01,534 --> 00:20:03,036
Or that thing in Joey's
refrigerator, remember?

491
00:20:03,077 --> 00:20:06,831
It was in a milk carton,
but it looked like meat?

492
00:20:06,873 --> 00:20:08,082
Come here. Come here.

493
00:20:08,124 --> 00:20:09,125
( gasps )

494
00:20:09,167 --> 00:20:10,751
There she is.

495
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:12,670
Hi.

496
00:20:12,712 --> 00:20:14,797
What?

497
00:20:14,839 --> 00:20:17,633
Nothing.

498
00:20:17,675 --> 00:20:20,636
Hi.

499
00:20:21,637 --> 00:20:23,222
Wh...?

500
00:20:30,897 --> 00:20:33,191
( gasping )

501
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:36,318
Please tell me
those are clip-ons.

502
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:38,236
Oh, they're real.

503
00:20:38,278 --> 00:20:40,322
Did she do this to her?

504
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:42,700
I told you we shouldn't

505
00:20:42,742 --> 00:20:44,368
have left Emma with her.
I know, I know,

506
00:20:44,410 --> 00:20:45,703
and you were
right, Ross, okay?

507
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:47,163
You are so irresponsible!

508
00:20:47,205 --> 00:20:49,498
I am never letting you
baby-sit ever again!

509
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:52,168
Hey, you know, what,
this kid needs me, okay?

510
00:20:52,210 --> 00:20:54,253
She needs to have
a cool, fun aunt.

511
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:55,713
I'm a cool, fun aunt.

512
00:20:55,755 --> 00:20:57,882
Okay.

513
00:20:57,924 --> 00:20:59,466
Hey!

514
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:03,804
Monica can be cool and fun
at organized, indoor projects!

515
00:21:04,847 --> 00:21:06,390
I cannot believe this.

516
00:21:06,432 --> 00:21:07,934
All I wanted to do was
help you try to figure out

517
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:09,143
what to do with your life,

518
00:21:09,185 --> 00:21:10,310
and this is how
you repay me?!

519
00:21:10,352 --> 00:21:12,105
Well, I don't need you
to help me

520
00:21:12,146 --> 00:21:14,356
because I already know what
I'm going to do with my life.

521
00:21:14,398 --> 00:21:16,067
Oh, yeah? Since when?

522
00:21:16,109 --> 00:21:18,236
Since today.

523
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:23,407
I am going to be a baby stylist.

524
00:21:24,450 --> 00:21:25,576
What?

525
00:21:25,618 --> 00:21:27,745
That's not a thing!

526
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:29,914
Well, it should be.

527
00:21:29,956 --> 00:21:33,042
I'm going to help babies
learn how to accessorize,

528
00:21:33,084 --> 00:21:36,837
what colors to wear,
what clothes are slimming.

529
00:21:36,879 --> 00:21:38,547
Babies don't care
if they're slim!

530
00:21:38,589 --> 00:21:40,507
Enter Amy.

531
00:21:41,592 --> 00:21:44,262
Amy, I j... I just...
I just want to...

532
00:21:44,303 --> 00:21:45,471
What? What are you doing to do?

533
00:21:46,513 --> 00:21:50,143
No more falafel for you!

534
00:22:02,113 --> 00:22:03,572
Oh, great game, huh?

535
00:22:03,614 --> 00:22:04,782
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

536
00:22:05,825 --> 00:22:08,077
Why do you keep
looking at the screen?

537
00:22:08,119 --> 00:22:09,245
I'm not.

538
00:22:09,287 --> 00:22:10,746
I-I'm praying.

539
00:22:10,788 --> 00:22:13,415
Please,
let the Knicks win.

540
00:22:13,457 --> 00:22:15,918
Thank you, Thor.

541
00:22:16,961 --> 00:22:18,087
Where are you going?

542
00:22:18,129 --> 00:22:19,421
Going to go to
the bathroom.

543
00:22:19,463 --> 00:22:20,923
Well, I think
you should wait.

544
00:22:20,965 --> 00:22:22,300
Why?

545
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:25,011
Well, if you don't...
if you don't hold it in,

546
00:22:25,052 --> 00:22:27,888
you don't... you don't get
all the nutrients.

547
00:22:27,930 --> 00:22:29,431
ANNOUNCER:
Knicks fans,

548
00:22:29,473 --> 00:22:32,059
can we turn your attention
to the big screen.

549
00:22:32,101 --> 00:22:35,562
Someone has a special question
to ask.

550
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:41,652
Mike Hannigan,
will you marry me?

551
00:22:42,695 --> 00:22:44,322
ANNOUNCER
Get a load of this.

552
00:22:44,362 --> 00:22:45,948
She's proposing to him.

553
00:22:45,990 --> 00:22:49,327
Guess we know who wears
the pants in that family.

554
00:22:50,368 --> 00:22:52,038
Well, that's not
very enlightened!

555
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:53,497
( crowd booing )

556
00:22:53,539 --> 00:22:54,874
Wuss!
Wimp!

557
00:22:54,915 --> 00:22:57,375
Hey! Hey!

558
00:22:57,417 --> 00:22:59,879
Boo us? Boo you!

559
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:02,380
( crowd booing )

560
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:05,301
( phone rings )

561
00:23:06,344 --> 00:23:07,761
Hello?

562
00:23:07,803 --> 00:23:10,597
Yeah, this is Joey Tribbiani.

563
00:23:10,639 --> 00:23:12,308
Oh, hi.

564
00:23:14,143 --> 00:23:16,729
Well, I'm glad
you liked my letter.

565
00:23:17,730 --> 00:23:22,068
No, my mommy and daddy
aren't home right now.

566
00:23:22,109 --> 00:23:24,528
Okay, bye-bye.

567
00:23:27,573 --> 00:23:30,784
She was nice.

568
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:32,245
Joey, get Amy's bags.

569
00:23:32,286 --> 00:23:33,537
She is moving out.

570
00:23:33,579 --> 00:23:35,039
Whoo-hoo!

571
00:23:35,081 --> 00:23:37,333
You're kicking me out?

572
00:23:37,375 --> 00:23:40,127
You put holes in my baby's ears.

573
00:23:40,169 --> 00:23:42,504
Yeah, well, at least now people
will know she's a girl.

574
00:23:42,546 --> 00:23:43,756
( gasps )

575
00:23:45,258 --> 00:23:46,884
I can't believe
I ever even tried

576
00:23:46,926 --> 00:23:48,052
to help you.

577
00:23:48,094 --> 00:23:50,388
You are so beyond help.

578
00:23:50,428 --> 00:23:52,014
You know what,
ever since I got here,

579
00:23:52,056 --> 00:23:53,557
you have been nothing
but negative.

580
00:23:53,599 --> 00:23:54,934
Excuse me?

581
00:23:54,975 --> 00:23:56,602
You didn't want me
to marry the old guy

582
00:23:56,643 --> 00:23:57,895
with the great apartment.

583
00:23:57,937 --> 00:23:59,563
Then, I try
to help your daughter

584
00:23:59,605 --> 00:24:01,774
de-emphasize her flaws...

585
00:24:03,567 --> 00:24:05,152
...and suddenly I'm the bad guy?

586
00:24:05,194 --> 00:24:06,570
Joey, where are those bags?

587
00:24:06,612 --> 00:24:08,030
JOEY:
She has a lot of crap!

588
00:24:08,072 --> 00:24:09,115
( groans )

589
00:24:09,156 --> 00:24:10,908
You know what?

590
00:24:10,950 --> 00:24:13,660
When I moved in here, I thought,
this is going to be so great.

591
00:24:13,702 --> 00:24:15,453
Just us sisters,
back together again,

592
00:24:15,495 --> 00:24:18,249
like when we were kids,
except without that stupid Jill.

593
00:24:18,291 --> 00:24:22,253
Oh, who has gotten fat,
by the way.

594
00:24:23,296 --> 00:24:24,255
Seriously?

595
00:24:24,297 --> 00:24:25,589
Mm-hmm.

596
00:24:25,631 --> 00:24:28,175
Mom said she gained,
like, 15 pounds.

597
00:24:28,217 --> 00:24:29,051
Hips or thighs?

598
00:24:29,093 --> 00:24:29,927
Ass and face.

599
00:24:29,969 --> 00:24:32,012
Oh!

600
00:24:32,054 --> 00:24:33,513
Oh, my God.

601
00:24:33,555 --> 00:24:35,391
I thought she was on Atkins.

602
00:24:35,433 --> 00:24:36,392
She was.

603
00:24:36,434 --> 00:24:37,559
Carbs found her.

604
00:24:41,105 --> 00:24:43,023
See?

605
00:24:43,065 --> 00:24:45,025
This is what I wanted.

606
00:24:45,067 --> 00:24:48,362
Two sisters talking
about real stuff.

607
00:24:50,406 --> 00:24:52,950
Oh, I can give you that.

608
00:24:52,992 --> 00:24:54,201
You can?

609
00:24:54,243 --> 00:24:55,661
Yeah.

610
00:24:55,702 --> 00:24:57,788
I kept trying to make
you a better person,

611
00:24:57,830 --> 00:25:00,540
but you're, you're already
a pretty perfect version

612
00:25:00,582 --> 00:25:02,126
of what you are.

613
00:25:02,168 --> 00:25:04,878
Thank you.

614
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:07,923
And you've got to admit,
Emma does look cute.

615
00:25:08,966 --> 00:25:11,051
Did you just say "Emma"?

616
00:25:11,093 --> 00:25:14,013
Oh, I'm sorry. Ella.

617
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:20,727
That woman at the
game didn't know

618
00:25:20,769 --> 00:25:23,105
what she was
talking about, Mike.

619
00:25:23,147 --> 00:25:25,024
Obviously,
you have balls.

620
00:25:26,025 --> 00:25:27,985
Well, please, let's just forget
the whole thing.

621
00:25:28,027 --> 00:25:29,153
I would love it.

622
00:25:29,195 --> 00:25:30,154
Consider it forgotten.

623
00:25:30,196 --> 00:25:31,280
Thank you.

624
00:25:31,322 --> 00:25:33,032
But just so you know,

625
00:25:33,073 --> 00:25:36,494
however and whenever
you decide to propose,

626
00:25:36,534 --> 00:25:39,497
I promise I'll say yes.

627
00:25:39,537 --> 00:25:41,999
Whether-whether, you know,
it's at a basketball game

628
00:25:42,041 --> 00:25:44,001
or in skywriting

629
00:25:44,043 --> 00:25:46,337
or, you know, like some
lame guy in a cheesy movie

630
00:25:46,379 --> 00:25:49,465
who hides it in the cake.

631
00:25:54,011 --> 00:25:56,554
It's in the cake, isn't it?

632
00:25:58,598 --> 00:26:02,102
Where else would lame,
Mr. No Balls hide it?

633
00:26:02,144 --> 00:26:04,271
What's the matter with me?

634
00:26:04,313 --> 00:26:05,523
Why do I keep
ruining this?

635
00:26:05,563 --> 00:26:06,524
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

636
00:26:06,606 --> 00:26:07,900
No, it's my fault.

637
00:26:07,941 --> 00:26:10,027
I keep trying to propose
in these stupid ways,

638
00:26:10,069 --> 00:26:12,196
and all I want to do
is tell you that I love you,

639
00:26:12,238 --> 00:26:14,907
and that I want to spend the
rest of my life with you and...

640
00:26:17,575 --> 00:26:20,538
I'm going to do this now.

641
00:26:20,578 --> 00:26:22,580
Oh, my God.

642
00:26:24,582 --> 00:26:26,710
Phoebe, I...

643
00:26:26,752 --> 00:26:28,462
Wait, oh, wait.

644
00:26:32,425 --> 00:26:34,592
Oh, no.

645
00:26:36,636 --> 00:26:39,056
Okay. Ooh.

646
00:26:39,098 --> 00:26:39,890
Ready?

647
00:26:39,932 --> 00:26:40,598
Uh-huh.

648
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:42,059
Okay.

649
00:26:44,228 --> 00:26:47,440
Phoebe, I love you.

650
00:26:49,483 --> 00:26:50,901
There's no one else
in the world

651
00:26:50,943 --> 00:26:52,570
I would ask to marry me
three times.

652
00:26:54,612 --> 00:26:57,199
But I want
to take care of you,

653
00:26:57,241 --> 00:26:58,992
have babies with you...

654
00:27:00,035 --> 00:27:03,080
...and grow old with you.

655
00:27:04,415 --> 00:27:07,751
Phoebe Buffay,
will you marry me?

656
00:27:08,794 --> 00:27:10,628
Yes.

657
00:27:16,385 --> 00:27:17,928
I love you.

658
00:27:17,970 --> 00:27:19,513
I love you more.

659
00:27:19,555 --> 00:27:20,889
Not possible.

660
00:27:29,440 --> 00:27:32,526
She's going to be
Mrs. No Balls.

661
00:27:39,283 --> 00:27:41,619
So, how's the, uh,
baby-styling business going?

662
00:27:41,659 --> 00:27:42,869
Not that great.

663
00:27:42,911 --> 00:27:44,704
It's... it's almost
as if people

664
00:27:44,746 --> 00:27:48,375
don't want to hear that
their babies are ugly.

665
00:27:48,417 --> 00:27:50,461
That's shocking.

666
00:27:50,503 --> 00:27:52,045
I know.

667
00:27:52,087 --> 00:27:53,297
Uh, there's Ross.

668
00:27:53,339 --> 00:27:54,548
Hey, Ross.

669
00:27:57,343 --> 00:28:00,471
Hello! Ross!

670
00:28:00,513 --> 00:28:03,432
( scoffs )
He's rude.

671
00:28:03,474 --> 00:28:07,186
